  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0077' consists of five tables: User, Product, Order, Announcement, and Order_Detail.\nThe User table represents a user of the system. It contains columns for Address_Details, Email, ID (which is the primary key), Membership_Number, Name, Password, Phone_Number, and Postal_Code.\nThe Product table holds information about the products. It includes columns for Category, Manufacturer, Name, Price, Product_ID (which is the primary key), and Product_Image_URL.\nThe Order table records user orders. It has columns for Delivery_Status, Order_ID (which is the primary key), Purchase_Date, and User_ID. The User_ID column is a foreign key referencing the ID column in the User table.\nThe Announcement table holds information about system announcements. It includes columns for Announcement_Number (which is the primary key), Content, Publisher_ID, Registration_Date, and Title. The Publisher_ID column is a foreign key referencing the ID column in the User table.\nFinally, the Order_Detail table records the details of each order. It includes columns for Order_ID, Product_ID, Purchase_Quantity. Both Order_ID and Product_ID are foreign keys referencing the Order_ID and Product_ID columns in the Order and Product tables respectively.",
  "gold_question": "\"The online shopping system needs to manage users, products, orders, announcements, and access control. The system must record each user's membership number, ID, name, password, email, phone number, postal code, and address details; product information must include product ID, name, price, category ID, manufacturer, and product image URL; the system supports order processing, documenting each order's purchase ID, product ID, membership number, quantity, purchase date, and delivery status. The bulletin board feature must record the announcement's number, title, content, registration date, and publisher ID, used for publishing and managing announcements, allowing users to view announcements.\"",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0077.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0077\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `membership_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address_details` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `manufacturer` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `product_image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `announcement_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_detail` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_detail_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_detail_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
